    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-state-machine.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Playing a state machine",
      "prov:value": "> **An agent could also play a (non-deterministic) state machine as a tool.\n> Managing state (kinda) during human/agentic discussion.** — the owner,\n> 2026-09-20",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-state-machine.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The non-determinism is in the TRANSITIONS, not the shape",
      "prov:value": "**That needed no change to the engine.** An exclusive gateway carrying\n`<cat-harness.processes:decision>` is computed and `workflow_complete` *refuses* a\nhand-supplied outcome; one without it already meant the caller supplies the\nanswer. The mechanism for a non-deterministic transition was there before\nanybody asked for one."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-state-machine.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What did need adding: saying that a judgement is deliberate",
      "prov:value": "Indistinguishable from the outside — the gap `cat-harness.processes:no-skill` closed for\nactivities, one element type along. So `<cat-harness.processes:judgement reason=\"…\"/>`, with\nthe same three rules: the reason is **required** and a declaration without one\ndoes not load; it is refused on anything but an exclusive gateway; and it is\nrefused **alongside** `cat-harness.processes:decision`, because a gateway claiming both that a\ntable decides it and that a person does leaves a reader unable to tell which\nthe author meant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-state-machine.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What did need adding: saying that a judgement is deliberate",
      "prov:value": "**Why this matters more than the activity case.** A step with no skill is a\ndocumentation gap. A gateway with no table is a point where an LLM decides the\nbranch — and *how many of those there are, and which*, is exactly the question\nthe deterministic-to-agentic spectrum is about (bean `q0tc`). **A mechanism\nthat cannot enumerate its own judgement points cannot answer it.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean q0tc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-state-machine.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "What did need adding: saying that a judgement is deliberate",
      "prov:value": "`check:workflow-refs` now prints the three-way split. Issue #200 §6 classified\nthis repository's decision points in prose, in an issue, where nothing reads\nit; the count is now printed from the models. **Ask the checker, not this\npage** — and note that an undeclared gateway is a backlog entry rather than a\ndefect: every one that predates the marker lands there, and a gate that failed\non an un-annotated corpus is a gate somebody turns off.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#200"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/session-state-machine.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two judgement points, and why each is safe to be one",
      "prov:value": "**That contrast is the shape of the answer `q0tc` is looking for**, and this\nskill deliberately does not pre-empt it: *recoverability* is one candidate\ncriterion for where judgement is admissible, tested on two gateways. Whether\nit is the right one, and what else belongs beside it, is research rather than\nassertion."
    }
  ]
}
